WEBVTT

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.344
You all right?

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.282
What time is it?

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.012
0400.

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.450
Your hearing starts
in four hours.

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:57.115
I suggest trying
to get some sleep.

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:59.182
You've got a big day
ahead of you.

00:03:03.981 --> 00:03:06.814
This hearing will come to order.

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:09.717
We are here to consider the
request of the Klingon Empire

00:03:09.753 --> 00:03:11.186
that Lieutenant Commander Worf

00:03:11.222 --> 00:03:13.952
be extradited for trial
on charges of murder.

00:03:13.991 --> 00:03:15.083
Advocate Ch'Pok.

00:03:15.125 --> 00:03:17.787
You may present your charges.

00:03:17.828 --> 00:03:20.695
The Klingon Empire makes
the following allegations

00:03:20.731 --> 00:03:22.961
against Lieutenant
Commander Worf:

00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:25.331
That on stardate 49648

00:03:25.369 --> 00:03:27.701
while commanding
the Starship Defiant

00:03:27.738 --> 00:03:29.899
he knowingly fired upon

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:32.932
and destroyed a Klingon
civilian transport ship

00:03:32.977 --> 00:03:35.104
near the Pentath system.

00:03:35.145 --> 00:03:37.238
That as a result of that action

00:03:37.281 --> 00:03:40.739
441 Klingon civilians
were killed.

00:03:40.784 --> 00:03:42.445
It is my intention to prove

00:03:42.486 --> 00:03:45.455
that Mr. Worf was
grossly negligent

00:03:45.489 --> 00:03:48.117
in his command of the Defiant.

00:03:48.158 --> 00:03:53.255
That his lust for combat
overrode his good judgment.

00:03:53.297 --> 00:03:57.097
I ask only that he
be returned to us

00:03:57.134 --> 00:04:00.865
to face the judgment
of his own people.

00:04:00.904 --> 00:04:03.498
Thank you.

00:04:08.979 --> 00:04:11.914
The Advocate
neglected to mention

00:04:11.949 --> 00:04:14.816
in his opening statement
that at the time in question

00:04:14.852 --> 00:04:18.720
the Defiant was under attack
by two Klingon warships.

00:04:18.756 --> 00:04:21.925
This was a combat situation
with hundreds of lives at stake.

00:04:22.058 --> 00:04:24.720
It was at that moment,
when suddenly

00:04:24.761 --> 00:04:27.389
the transport ship de-cloaked
in front of the Defiant.

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:28.863
Worf gave the order to fire.

00:04:28.898 --> 00:04:32.766
Not because he was
reckless or negligent

00:04:32.802 --> 00:04:35.828
but because he believed
he was firing on a warship.

00:04:35.872 --> 00:04:39.899
We intend to show that the
destruction of the transport

00:04:39.943 --> 00:04:43.504
was a tragic
but unavoidable accident.

00:04:45.581 --> 00:04:47.242
I will hear formal evidence

00:04:47.283 --> 00:04:50.446
beginning tomorrow afternoon
at 1500 hours.

00:04:56.693 --> 00:04:58.820
I want to know everything
there is to know

00:04:58.861 --> 00:05:01.421
about the Klingon who was
commanding that transport ship.

00:05:01.464 --> 00:05:04.092
You suspect it wasn't
just an innocent passenger run.

00:05:04.133 --> 00:05:06.363
I'm going to argue
that he saw the battle

00:05:06.402 --> 00:05:08.063
and then decided to join it

00:05:08.104 --> 00:05:10.629
that he de-cloaked in order
to attack the Defiant.

00:05:10.673 --> 00:05:12.800
Not the smartest decision
he ever made.

00:05:12.842 --> 00:05:14.537
That's where you come in.

00:05:14.577 --> 00:05:16.044
Use your contacts in the Empire

00:05:16.079 --> 00:05:18.639
and find out something
about this Captain I can use.

00:05:18.681 --> 00:05:19.841
Was he reckless?

00:05:19.882 --> 00:05:21.747
Did he have a reputation
for drinking?

00:05:21.784 --> 00:05:23.775
Did he have a death wish?
Something.

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:25.947
I'll see what I can do.

00:05:28.324 --> 00:05:29.985
Captain.

00:05:31.728 --> 00:05:33.855
The witnesses I intend to call.

00:05:33.896 --> 00:05:36.228
Thank you.

00:05:36.265 --> 00:05:38.961
A remarkable station, Captain.

00:05:39.068 --> 00:05:40.126
Thank you.

00:05:40.169 --> 00:05:42.637
We don't get many Klingon
visitors anymore.

00:05:42.672 --> 00:05:43.730
After this case is over

00:05:43.773 --> 00:05:45.468
you might be seeing
a lot more of us.

00:05:45.508 --> 00:05:47.100
Oh?

00:05:47.143 --> 00:05:49.509
When Worf is extradited

00:05:49.545 --> 00:05:51.570
the Federation
will be forced to admit

00:05:51.614 --> 00:05:53.946
that one of its officers
committed a massacre.

00:05:53.983 --> 00:05:55.610
That will put you
on the defensive

00:05:55.651 --> 00:05:56.845
throughout the Quadrant.

00:05:56.886 --> 00:05:58.979
And while you're busy
trying to repair

00:05:59.088 --> 00:06:01.352
a badly damaged reputation

00:06:01.391 --> 00:06:04.019
we'll find ourselves
with certain...

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:06.551
opportunities.

00:06:06.596 --> 00:06:10.327
An opportunity to annex
more Cardassian space

00:06:10.366 --> 00:06:13.301
and set up additional
military bases in this sector?

00:06:13.336 --> 00:06:14.667
Possibly.

00:06:14.704 --> 00:06:17.935
But in any case,
Worf is about to present us

00:06:17.974 --> 00:06:20.636
with something we never
could have won in battle.

00:06:20.676 --> 00:06:22.166
Sympathy.

00:06:22.211 --> 00:06:24.236
Any move we make against you

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:26.805
will be seen
as a legitimate response

00:06:26.849 --> 00:06:28.749
to an outrageous slaughter.

00:06:28.785 --> 00:06:30.480
You're presuming an awful lot.

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:32.385
Worf maintains his innocence.

00:06:32.422 --> 00:06:34.856
And you're about to remind me

00:06:34.891 --> 00:06:37.519
that the burden
of proof is mine.

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:41.587
It's an interesting system
of justice you have, Captain.

00:06:41.631 --> 00:06:43.758
It does have its flaws, however.

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:47.759
It emphasizes procedure
over substance

00:06:47.804 --> 00:06:50.272
form over fact.

00:06:50.306 --> 00:06:53.241
I'm sorry if you feel it
puts you at a disadvantage.

00:06:53.276 --> 00:06:54.766
On the contrary.

00:06:54.811 --> 00:06:57.371
I look forward
to fighting on your terms.

00:06:57.413 --> 00:06:58.971
This is not a fight.

00:06:59.048 --> 00:07:01.073
It's the search for the truth.

00:07:02.051 --> 00:07:05.509
The truth must be won.

00:07:05.555 --> 00:07:08.581
I'll see you
on the battlefield.

00:07:15.064 --> 00:07:17.589
I have studied
Commander Worf's reports

00:07:17.633 --> 00:07:19.225
the Defiant's sensor logs

00:07:19.268 --> 00:07:22.431
and the reports of the
other officers on the Bridge.

00:07:22.472 --> 00:07:24.940
And I believe every word of it.

00:07:25.041 --> 00:07:28.306
It's a matter of pride
for the Federation

00:07:28.344 --> 00:07:30.938
that Starfleet officers
never lie or commit fraud.

00:07:31.013 --> 00:07:33.379
So I will accept
the facts of the case

00:07:33.416 --> 00:07:35.509
as they have been submitted.

00:07:35.551 --> 00:07:39.578
Admiral, if there are
no facts in dispute

00:07:39.622 --> 00:07:43.422
then this hearing would
appear to be at an end.

00:07:43.459 --> 00:07:46.690
We Klingons are not concerned

00:07:46.729 --> 00:07:49.197
with matters of fact
and circumstance.

00:07:49.232 --> 00:07:51.291
What matters to us
is what was in Worf's heart

00:07:51.334 --> 00:07:52.699
when he gave the order to fire.

00:07:52.735 --> 00:07:55.363
Was he just a Starfleet officer

00:07:55.404 --> 00:07:58.168
doing his duty,
or was he a Klingon warrior

00:07:58.207 --> 00:07:59.640
reveling in the battle?

00:07:59.675 --> 00:08:01.802
That is why I am here.

00:08:01.844 --> 00:08:03.903
Because if he was a Klingon

00:08:04.013 --> 00:08:06.777
Iost in the bloodlust
of combat

00:08:06.816 --> 00:08:10.912
only we can judge him, not you.

00:08:10.953 --> 00:08:14.150
We can't put a man's
heart on trial.

00:08:14.190 --> 00:08:15.555
It's a subjective issue

00:08:15.591 --> 00:08:17.684
that cannot be reasoned
in a court of law.

00:08:17.727 --> 00:08:20.355
I ask that the Advocate
be limited

00:08:20.396 --> 00:08:23.024
to arguing the evidence
in this case.

00:08:23.065 --> 00:08:25.693
Someone told me this was
a search for the truth.

00:08:25.735 --> 00:08:29.933
Should we not follow that search
wherever it takes us?

00:08:29.972 --> 00:08:34.306
The question of Commander Worf's
motive is relevant.

00:08:34.343 --> 00:08:37.642
I will allow you
to explore this issue

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:40.945
but only as far
as logic permits.

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:43.348
I bow to your judgment.

00:08:43.386 --> 00:08:47.880
You may call your first witness.

00:08:47.924 --> 00:08:49.858
You are considered
something of an expert

00:08:49.892 --> 00:08:52.622
on Klingon society,
aren't you, Commander?

00:08:52.662 --> 00:08:56.393
My previous host, Curzon, would
have called himself an expert.

00:08:56.432 --> 00:08:57.899
I tend to think of myself

00:08:57.934 --> 00:09:00.903
as having a passing familiarity
with your culture.

00:09:00.937 --> 00:09:03.872
In your opinion,
as someone with a...

00:09:03.906 --> 00:09:06.704
passing familiarity
with our culture

00:09:06.742 --> 00:09:11.042
wouldn't you say the Klingons
are a violent, warrior race?

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:14.140
Yes, there is that aspect
to your people.

00:09:14.183 --> 00:09:16.014
Would you agree
that one of the things

00:09:16.052 --> 00:09:18.520
that makes a Klingon warrior
so formidable

00:09:18.554 --> 00:09:22.923
is his predatory instinct,
his blood lust, if you will?

00:09:22.959 --> 00:09:24.927
I'd agree with that.

00:09:24.994 --> 00:09:27.690
Now, when Worf
was on the Defiant

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:29.698
engaged in combat,
don't you think

00:09:29.732 --> 00:09:32.098
his predatory instinct
took over?

00:09:32.134 --> 00:09:35.331
I think that instinct
was present

00:09:35.371 --> 00:09:38.033
but I've seen Mr. Worf
restrain it before.

00:09:38.074 --> 00:09:40.304
How do you know so much
about how he behaves in battle?

00:09:40.343 --> 00:09:42.937
In the holosuite,
we've fought many times.

00:09:42.979 --> 00:09:46.244
You mean you practiced
with Mr. Worf.

00:09:46.282 --> 00:09:47.943
You played with him.

00:09:48.017 --> 00:09:49.848
Oh, no.

00:09:49.885 --> 00:09:52.945
When we fight, we fight.

00:09:53.055 --> 00:09:55.421
I've made it very clear
to Mr. Worf

00:09:55.458 --> 00:09:58.791
that I never want him
to take it easy on me

00:09:58.828 --> 00:10:00.796
because I'm a woman or a Trill.

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:02.559
Have you ever been injured?

00:10:02.598 --> 00:10:04.395
A few bruises here and there.

00:10:04.433 --> 00:10:06.367
A broken finger once.

00:10:06.402 --> 00:10:09.166
Nothing serious,
and I've given him

00:10:09.205 --> 00:10:10.900
a few lumps of his own.

00:10:12.375 --> 00:10:15.538
So you're not afraid
of Mr. Worf.

00:10:15.578 --> 00:10:16.977
I'm no fool.

00:10:17.013 --> 00:10:19.174
I can see the killer instinct
in his eyes.

00:10:19.215 --> 00:10:22.707
And I know he could
kill me if he wants to.

00:10:22.752 --> 00:10:25.186
But that look always goes away.

00:10:25.221 --> 00:10:27.155
He knows when to stop.

00:10:27.189 --> 00:10:29.157
Jadt.

00:10:29.191 --> 00:10:30.556
Admiral, at this time

00:10:30.593 --> 00:10:33.994
I would like to enter into
evidence files I obtained

00:10:34.096 --> 00:10:36.155
from the defendant's private
data base this morning.

00:10:36.198 --> 00:10:37.324
Objection.

00:10:37.366 --> 00:10:39.960
There's been no search order
issued for those files.

00:10:40.002 --> 00:10:42.527
This is a violation
of Mr. Worf's privacy.

00:10:42.571 --> 00:10:44.334
The Captain is correct.

00:10:44.373 --> 00:10:46.739
Without a properly
executed search order

00:10:46.776 --> 00:10:48.641
or the permission of the
defendant, any information

00:10:48.678 --> 00:10:51.340
you have accessed
from his private data base

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:53.940
may not be admitted
into evidence.

00:10:53.983 --> 00:10:55.450
Ah. I see.

00:10:55.484 --> 00:10:57.918
Well, I obviously
have no search order

00:10:57.953 --> 00:11:01.047
so I'll ask you, Worf.

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:03.149
May I enter this file
into evidence

00:11:03.192 --> 00:11:06.093
or do you have
something to hide?

00:11:06.128 --> 00:11:07.959
Don't play his game.

00:11:07.997 --> 00:11:09.828
I have nothing to hide.

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:13.798
Use whatever you wish.

00:11:16.005 --> 00:11:18.303
Commander Dax, are you familiar

00:11:18.341 --> 00:11:21.469
with the holosuite program known
as "The Battle of Tong Vey"?

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:23.603
Yes.
It's one of the programs

00:11:23.646 --> 00:11:26.342
Mr. Worf brought with him
from the Enterprise.

00:11:26.382 --> 00:11:27.949
Describe it for us.

00:11:28.082 --> 00:11:29.947
It's an historical reenactment

00:11:29.984 --> 00:11:32.282
of one
of the epic Klingon battles.

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:35.915
10,000 warriors under the
command of Emperor Sompek

00:11:35.957 --> 00:11:39.859
conquer the city of Tong Vey
after a long siege.

00:11:39.894 --> 00:11:42.328
A glorious battle.

00:11:42.363 --> 00:11:45.890
When Worf recreates it
in the holosuite

00:11:45.933 --> 00:11:47.924
what role does he play?

00:11:47.969 --> 00:11:50.267
Sompek.

00:11:50.304 --> 00:11:52.636
Of course.
The conqueror's role.

00:11:52.673 --> 00:11:54.664
One of our greatest heroes.

00:11:54.709 --> 00:11:57.507
Tell me, Commander.

00:11:57.545 --> 00:12:00.241
What was the final order
Sompek gave to his men

00:12:00.281 --> 00:12:03.148
once they had conquered
the city of Tong Vey?

00:12:10.124 --> 00:12:11.421
Commander?

00:12:14.328 --> 00:12:16.558
He told them to burn
the city to the ground

00:12:16.597 --> 00:12:17.894
and kill everyone in it.

00:12:17.932 --> 00:12:20.264
Everyone?

00:12:20.301 --> 00:12:25.762
Not just the soldiers,
but the people of the town, too?

00:12:27.641 --> 00:12:29.404
Civilians?

00:12:29.443 --> 00:12:30.967
Women?

00:12:31.078 --> 00:12:33.069
Children?

00:12:33.114 --> 00:12:35.582
Yes.

00:12:35.616 --> 00:12:37.846
Now, Commander

00:12:37.885 --> 00:12:43.380
when Mr. Worf runs this program,
does he give the final order

00:12:43.424 --> 00:12:47.087
to destroy the city
and kill all of the inhabitants?

00:12:48.429 --> 00:12:50.420
It's not the same thing.

00:12:50.464 --> 00:12:52.091
It's a simulation...

00:12:52.133 --> 00:12:53.760
Answer the question.

00:12:59.273 --> 00:13:01.241
That's the way the program
is supposed to end.

00:13:01.275 --> 00:13:02.708
You have to give that command...

00:13:02.743 --> 00:13:03.869
Admiral

00:13:03.911 --> 00:13:05.572
I ask that the witness
be instructed

00:13:05.613 --> 00:13:08.104
to answer the question
"yes" or "no."

00:13:08.149 --> 00:13:09.946
Yes or no, Commander.

00:13:15.656 --> 00:13:16.623
Yes.

00:13:16.657 --> 00:13:18.318
Of course he does.

00:13:18.359 --> 00:13:20.418
Because he is
a Klingon warrior.

00:13:20.461 --> 00:13:21.428
He doesn't have

00:13:21.462 --> 00:13:23.657
the same moral code
as a Starfleet officer.

00:13:23.697 --> 00:13:26.860
He is one of us...
a killer, a predator

00:13:26.901 --> 00:13:28.061
among sheep.

00:13:28.102 --> 00:13:29.069
Objection!

00:13:29.103 --> 00:13:30.730
Restrain yourself, Advocate.

00:13:34.742 --> 00:13:38.143
I have only one more
question for this witness

00:13:38.179 --> 00:13:39.771
Admiral.

00:13:41.449 --> 00:13:44.247
Commander Dax

00:13:44.285 --> 00:13:50.121
when was the last time
Worf used that program?

00:13:58.165 --> 00:14:00.463
The day before he left
on the convoy mission.

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:11.844
The day before.
The day before.

00:14:14.014 --> 00:14:16.812
I have nothing further.

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:33.391
Captain, you ordered Worf
to command the Defiant

00:14:33.434 --> 00:14:35.698
on the mission in question,
did you not?

00:14:35.736 --> 00:14:37.397
That's right.

00:14:40.141 --> 00:14:42.803
How did you describe
the mission to Worf?

00:14:42.843 --> 00:14:44.674
An outbreak of Rudellian plague

00:14:44.712 --> 00:14:47.442
has struck the Cardassian colony
on Pentath III.

00:14:47.481 --> 00:14:49.574
The Cardassians are
preparing several convoys

00:14:49.617 --> 00:14:51.380
of medical supplies
and relief workers

00:14:51.418 --> 00:14:54.444
but the Pentath system
borders Klingon territory

00:14:54.488 --> 00:14:58.390
and the Cardassians
are worried about raids.

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:02.793
Well, Pentath is a strategically
important system.

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:05.355
The Klingons will
try to stop them.

00:15:05.399 --> 00:15:08.425
The problem is the Cardassians
don't have enough warships

00:15:08.469 --> 00:15:10.835
available to protect
the relief convoy.

00:15:10.871 --> 00:15:12.805
They've asked
for Starfleet protection

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:16.298
and because of the humanitarian
nature of the request

00:15:16.343 --> 00:15:17.867
we've agreed.

00:15:17.912 --> 00:15:21.643
There will be seven convoys
headed for Pentath III

00:15:21.682 --> 00:15:22.740
in the next week.

00:15:22.783 --> 00:15:25.183
Each of them protected
by a Federation starship.

00:15:25.219 --> 00:15:28.484
The Defiant has been assigned
to escort convoy six

00:15:28.522 --> 00:15:30.956
and I've chosen you
to be in command.

00:15:31.025 --> 00:15:35.189
Why did you select Worf
for this mission?

00:15:35.229 --> 00:15:38.596
I felt that he was
an experienced officer

00:15:38.632 --> 00:15:42.966
who was ready to take on
greater responsibilities.

00:15:43.070 --> 00:15:44.594
He had a distinguished record

00:15:44.638 --> 00:15:47.072
and obviously understood
the Klingons.

00:15:47.107 --> 00:15:50.304
Weren't you a little worried,
Captain, that Worf...

00:15:50.344 --> 00:15:52.471
a famed Klingon warrior...

00:15:52.513 --> 00:15:54.879
might jump at the chance
for combat

00:15:54.915 --> 00:15:57.475
and forget about
the plague victims?

00:15:57.518 --> 00:16:00.214
If I were, I wouldn't
have given him the assignment.

00:16:00.254 --> 00:16:03.155
And you're sure you
made your instructions

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:05.784
perfectly clear...
that Commander Worf

00:16:05.826 --> 00:16:08.454
knew he was
on a humanitarian relief mission

00:16:08.495 --> 00:16:11.692
that he was not being
sent out to seek combat?

00:16:11.732 --> 00:16:12.790
Yes.

00:16:12.833 --> 00:16:13.800
Thank you, Captain.

00:16:13.834 --> 00:16:15.392
I have nothing further for you.

00:16:17.671 --> 00:16:20.936
Captain, since you are
also acting as defense counsel

00:16:21.041 --> 00:16:23.635
if you wish to add anything
to the record

00:16:23.677 --> 00:16:25.406
you're free to do so.

00:16:25.446 --> 00:16:27.243
Not at this time, Admiral.

00:16:27.281 --> 00:16:29.715
Call your next witness.

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:32.344
It was about 1700 hours.

00:16:32.386 --> 00:16:34.320
I was doing some cleanup work.

00:16:34.355 --> 00:16:37.620
Dr. Bashir was at the bar
talking to Etheria

00:16:37.658 --> 00:16:39.216
one of the dabo girls.

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:42.229
Have you ever seen
the wormhole open?

00:16:42.263 --> 00:16:43.355
No, wait.

00:16:43.397 --> 00:16:45.422
It wasn't Etheria;
it was Glidia.

00:16:45.466 --> 00:16:49.562
Have you ever seen
the wormhole open?

00:16:49.603 --> 00:16:54.233
Or was it... Midia?

00:16:54.275 --> 00:16:56.709
Mr. Quark, is this necess...?

00:16:56.744 --> 00:17:01.704
No, no. No, it was Ralidia,
and she was with Morn

00:17:01.749 --> 00:17:04.741
and he was the one
who turned to her and said...

00:17:04.785 --> 00:17:08.050
Can we get back
to the matter at hand, please?

00:17:08.088 --> 00:17:09.783
Oh, right.

00:17:09.823 --> 00:17:11.916
Um... well, as I said

00:17:11.992 --> 00:17:14.586
I was cleaning up,
and I saw Mr. Worf come in.

00:17:14.628 --> 00:17:18.496
Was there anything unusual
about that?

00:17:18.532 --> 00:17:21.126
No. He comes in here
all the time.

00:17:21.168 --> 00:17:24.831
But he was in a good mood.

00:17:24.872 --> 00:17:26.032
And that's unusual?

00:17:26.073 --> 00:17:27.938
Well, he's a Klingon

00:17:28.042 --> 00:17:31.375
and you people are rarely
in what I would call good moods

00:17:31.412 --> 00:17:37.078
not that you're anything
but a pleasant, charming race.

00:17:37.117 --> 00:17:39.347
Let's get back to Mr. Worf.

00:17:39.386 --> 00:17:41.047
Describe what happened next.

00:17:41.088 --> 00:17:45.923
He came in, he ordered a drink...
prune juice, I believe...

00:17:45.959 --> 00:17:47.859
and we started to talk.

00:17:47.895 --> 00:17:50.955
I'd heard
about the convoy mission

00:17:51.065 --> 00:17:52.555
so I asked him about it

00:17:52.599 --> 00:17:56.126
and he said he was going
to be commanding the Defiant.

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:57.728
What was his attitude?

00:18:00.207 --> 00:18:01.469
Hard to say.

00:18:01.508 --> 00:18:04.807
He's a very private man.

00:18:04.845 --> 00:18:07.712
He doesn't share a lot
with his bartender.

00:18:07.748 --> 00:18:09.807
Did he seem...

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:12.148
afraid of the mission?

00:18:12.186 --> 00:18:13.915
No.

00:18:14.021 --> 00:18:15.921
Did he seem excited
by the mission?

00:18:16.023 --> 00:18:19.618
Not excited exactly.

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:21.924
Then what exactly?

00:18:21.995 --> 00:18:24.623
I just remember asking him...

00:18:24.665 --> 00:18:28.601
What happens if the Klingons
go after the convoy?

00:18:28.635 --> 00:18:31.661
And then he got this
funny look on his face.

00:18:31.705 --> 00:18:33.366
He put down his prune juice

00:18:33.407 --> 00:18:36.934
Iooked me right in the eye,
and then he said...

00:18:37.044 --> 00:18:39.740
I hope they do.

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:41.509
"I hope they do."

00:18:41.548 --> 00:18:43.778
Well, it would appear

00:18:43.817 --> 00:18:46.386
Commander Worf's hopes
were answered.

00:18:46.519 --> 00:18:48.544
I have nothing further.

00:18:57.663 --> 00:18:59.756
What do you have
for me, Constable?

00:18:59.799 --> 00:19:02.427
Background on
the Klingon transport captain.

00:19:02.468 --> 00:19:04.368
He'd never been in the military

00:19:04.404 --> 00:19:06.167
and he was known
to his family and friends

00:19:06.205 --> 00:19:09.231
as a quiet, efficient man
who was content in his position.

00:19:09.275 --> 00:19:11.266
Doesn't sound like a man

00:19:11.310 --> 00:19:13.437
who'd suddenly decide
to take on the Defiant.

00:19:13.479 --> 00:19:14.878
No.

00:19:14.914 --> 00:19:17.906
What about this story of theirs
that the transport ship

00:19:17.984 --> 00:19:20.509
just wandered off course
into a combat area?

00:19:20.553 --> 00:19:23.147
I checked the flight plan
the Captain filed

00:19:23.189 --> 00:19:26.022
and the projected course
was near the border.

00:19:26.058 --> 00:19:29.494
It would have taken only a
very slight error in navigation

00:19:29.529 --> 00:19:32.089
for the ship to stray
into the fight.

00:19:32.131 --> 00:19:34.497
But why did he drop his cloak
right in front of the Defiant?

00:19:34.534 --> 00:19:37.526
Ah, that's the question
no one seems able to answer.

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:41.836
No one seems able,
or no one seems willing?

00:19:41.874 --> 00:19:43.466
Oh, they're too willing

00:19:43.509 --> 00:19:45.443
to answer questions...
that's the problem.

00:19:45.478 --> 00:19:47.503
I'm always suspicious of people

00:19:47.547 --> 00:19:50.038
who are eager to help
a police officer.

00:19:50.082 --> 00:19:53.415
Start looking into
the passengers on that ship.

00:19:53.453 --> 00:19:55.683
Maybe someone with a grudge
against Worf

00:19:55.721 --> 00:19:57.348
or the Federation was aboard...

00:19:57.390 --> 00:19:59.187
someone who could have
seized control

00:19:59.225 --> 00:20:01.318
of the ship and taken
it into the battle.

00:20:01.360 --> 00:20:03.794
I'm reaching, I know.

00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:06.230
But at the moment,
it's all we have.

00:20:06.265 --> 00:20:08.529
I'll keep looking.

00:20:08.568 --> 00:20:10.092
There were two Klingon ships...

00:20:10.136 --> 00:20:12.161
a bird-of-prey
and an old battle cruiser.

00:20:12.205 --> 00:20:14.935
One would engage us while
the other went after the convoy.

00:20:14.974 --> 00:20:16.134
Then they'd switch.

00:20:16.175 --> 00:20:18.200
The first ship going
after the Cardassians

00:20:18.244 --> 00:20:20.041
while the second ship
came after us.

00:20:24.550 --> 00:20:27.144
We've lost the number three
starboard shield.

00:20:27.186 --> 00:20:28.448
Come about.

00:20:28.488 --> 00:20:30.979
The cruiser has taken us
too far away from the convoy.

00:20:31.057 --> 00:20:33.184
Try to keep our port side
to the Klingons.

00:20:33.226 --> 00:20:34.523
Aye, sir.

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:38.326
This went on for... I don't know,
maybe five minutes.

00:20:38.364 --> 00:20:40.764
They'd come at us, try to draw
us away from the Cardassians.

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:42.131
We'd head back.

00:20:42.168 --> 00:20:45.069
Then the bird-of-prey came
toward us off the port bow.

00:20:49.108 --> 00:20:50.336
I have phaser lock.

00:20:50.376 --> 00:20:51.775
Fire.

00:20:55.314 --> 00:20:57.441
We damaged them but not much.

00:20:57.483 --> 00:21:00.350
We'd seen them do this cloak-
and-run maneuver a few times

00:21:00.386 --> 00:21:02.411
and Commander Worf
thought he saw a pattern.

00:21:02.455 --> 00:21:04.685
We have them now.

00:21:04.724 --> 00:21:07.124
Come to course 185 mark 278.

00:21:07.159 --> 00:21:09.286
Stand by quantum
torpedoes, full spread.

00:21:09.328 --> 00:21:10.556
Aye, sir.

00:21:10.596 --> 00:21:13.759
I ran a quick sensor sweep
then I reported.

00:21:13.799 --> 00:21:16.165
I'm picking up a tachyon surge
directly ahead.

00:21:16.202 --> 00:21:17.191
Fire.

00:21:21.007 --> 00:21:24.636
When did you realize
it wasn't a bird-of-prey?

00:21:24.677 --> 00:21:26.372
As soon as it exploded.

00:21:26.412 --> 00:21:27.811
Oh, my God.

00:21:27.847 --> 00:21:29.474
We were all stunned.

00:21:29.515 --> 00:21:32.279
I scanned for survivors,
but there were none.

00:21:32.318 --> 00:21:34.411
Chief, do you believe

00:21:34.453 --> 00:21:36.944
Worf was correct
in giving the order to fire?

00:21:36.989 --> 00:21:38.980
I stand by his decision.

00:21:39.091 --> 00:21:42.356
Is there any question
in your mind about his motives?

00:21:42.395 --> 00:21:43.794
No, sir.

00:21:43.829 --> 00:21:46.992
I've known Commander Worf
for nine years.

00:21:47.033 --> 00:21:48.762
He's an honorable man.

00:21:48.801 --> 00:21:51.395
He would never intentionally
fire on an unarmed ship.

00:21:51.437 --> 00:21:52.927
Thank you, Chief.

00:21:58.344 --> 00:22:00.642
I'm curious, Chief.

00:22:00.680 --> 00:22:04.639
You say you stand by
Commander Worf's decision.

00:22:04.684 --> 00:22:06.174
Do you agree with it?

00:22:06.218 --> 00:22:09.153
I completely support him.

00:22:09.188 --> 00:22:10.849
That's not my question.

00:22:10.890 --> 00:22:13.358
Do you agree with his decision?

00:22:13.392 --> 00:22:15.690
I wasn't in command.

00:22:15.728 --> 00:22:18.526
It's not my place
to question his judgment.

00:22:18.564 --> 00:22:20.293
What if you were in command?

00:22:20.333 --> 00:22:21.891
What would you have done?

00:22:23.970 --> 00:22:25.835
I don't know.

00:22:25.871 --> 00:22:30.240
Chief, how many years have
you been in Starfleet?

00:22:30.276 --> 00:22:31.675
Twenty-two.

00:22:31.711 --> 00:22:34.703
And how many combat
situations have you been in?

00:22:34.747 --> 00:22:37.238
I couldn't even guess.

00:22:37.283 --> 00:22:38.614
Try.

00:22:40.386 --> 00:22:42.115
100, 150.

00:22:42.154 --> 00:22:43.553
For the record

00:22:43.589 --> 00:22:47.355
Chief O'Brien has been
in 235 separate engagements

00:22:47.393 --> 00:22:50.885
and Starfleet
has decorated him 15 times.

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:53.899
I would like to have him
declared an expert

00:22:53.933 --> 00:22:55.992
in the area of starship combat.

00:22:56.102 --> 00:22:57.660
Any objection?

00:22:57.703 --> 00:22:59.967
None.

00:23:00.006 --> 00:23:04.705
Chief O'Brien,
if Mr. Worf had been injured

00:23:04.744 --> 00:23:07.645
could you have taken over
command of that ship?

00:23:07.680 --> 00:23:09.409
I would have.

00:23:09.448 --> 00:23:11.348
Let's say that happened.

00:23:11.384 --> 00:23:13.545
You're in command.

00:23:13.586 --> 00:23:16.214
You're chasing the bird-of-prey.

00:23:16.255 --> 00:23:17.222
It cloaks.

00:23:17.256 --> 00:23:19.451
You anticipate
your opponent's maneuver

00:23:19.492 --> 00:23:21.858
so you give the order.

00:23:21.894 --> 00:23:24.226
Come about to 185 mark 278.

00:23:24.263 --> 00:23:27.391
Stand by quantum torpedoes,
full spread.

00:23:27.433 --> 00:23:28.866
The crew obeys.

00:23:28.901 --> 00:23:30.266
The ship comes about.

00:23:30.302 --> 00:23:32.736
And then your helm officer
tells you...

00:23:32.772 --> 00:23:35.639
I'm picking up a tachyon surge,
directly ahead.

00:23:35.675 --> 00:23:36.835
Now, stop right there.

00:23:36.876 --> 00:23:38.741
Freeze that moment in time.

00:23:38.778 --> 00:23:41.474
Everything rides
on your next decision.

00:23:41.514 --> 00:23:43.982
Do you give the order to fire?

00:23:44.016 --> 00:23:45.745
This isn't a fair question.

00:23:45.785 --> 00:23:47.480
It didn't really happen
this way.

00:23:47.520 --> 00:23:49.488
I wasn't in command.

00:23:49.522 --> 00:23:51.251
I'm not interested
in whether you think

00:23:51.290 --> 00:23:52.450
it's a fair question or not.

00:23:52.491 --> 00:23:54.083
You're in command.

00:23:54.126 --> 00:23:56.219
There's a ship out there
de-cloaking.

00:23:56.262 --> 00:23:58.127
You don't know what it is.

00:23:58.164 --> 00:23:59.688
Do you fire?

00:24:07.306 --> 00:24:08.568
No.

00:24:10.743 --> 00:24:13.871
But that's just my opinion now,
after the fact.

00:24:13.913 --> 00:24:16.643
I wasn't in command that day.

00:24:16.682 --> 00:24:20.311
Things look a lot different when
you're sitting in that chair.

00:24:25.357 --> 00:24:27.825
I'm sure they do.

00:24:48.214 --> 00:24:50.079
Captain Sisko

00:24:50.116 --> 00:24:53.415
mind if I sit down?

00:25:03.195 --> 00:25:05.288
I understand
you're going to put Worf

00:25:05.331 --> 00:25:06.923
on the stand this afternoon.

00:25:06.966 --> 00:25:08.558
That's right.

00:25:08.601 --> 00:25:10.159
May I make a suggestion?

00:25:12.104 --> 00:25:13.867
Concede.

00:25:13.906 --> 00:25:16.374
Let me take him back
to the Empire

00:25:16.408 --> 00:25:18.467
and I'll make sure
he's not put to death.

00:25:18.511 --> 00:25:21.503
In fact, I'll defend him myself.

00:25:21.547 --> 00:25:22.605
You?

00:25:22.648 --> 00:25:23.808
What matters to me

00:25:23.849 --> 00:25:27.376
is the thrill of the fight,
not which side I'm on.

00:25:27.419 --> 00:25:31.651
And I think we both know
the extradition fight is over.

00:25:31.690 --> 00:25:34.284
You're not making
this offer out of kindness.

00:25:34.326 --> 00:25:36.487
You want the Federation
to concede

00:25:36.529 --> 00:25:38.429
so the convoys will stop

00:25:38.464 --> 00:25:42.901
and the Klingons can move in
on the Pentath system.

00:25:42.935 --> 00:25:48.874
As humans would say,
that would be icing on the cake.

00:25:48.908 --> 00:25:53.777
I wouldn't try eating that cake
just yet, if I were you.

00:25:56.015 --> 00:25:59.382
But you have told me one thing
I needed to know...

00:26:01.554 --> 00:26:05.823
you're worried about what Worf
might say on the stand.

00:26:05.956 --> 00:26:11.189
I'm not worried,
but you should be.

00:26:27.110 --> 00:26:29.271
Captain.

00:26:32.783 --> 00:26:34.307
Good news or bad?

00:26:34.351 --> 00:26:37.320
Bad. I checked the backgrounds

00:26:37.354 --> 00:26:39.117
of every passenger
on that transport.

00:26:39.156 --> 00:26:40.953
None had any connection
with Worf

00:26:41.024 --> 00:26:43.151
or grudge against the Federation

00:26:43.193 --> 00:26:46.094
or any motive
for seizing control

00:26:46.129 --> 00:26:48.290
of the ship
and attacking the Defiant.

00:26:48.332 --> 00:26:50.459
But I'm still not giving up.

00:26:50.500 --> 00:26:52.730
I appreciate that

00:26:52.769 --> 00:26:54.862
but I get the feeling
that at this point

00:26:54.905 --> 00:26:58.397
the only one who can
help Worf is Worf.

00:27:08.752 --> 00:27:11.482
The escort mission had
proceeded smoothly for two days.

00:27:11.521 --> 00:27:13.751
We detected
several subspace distortions

00:27:13.790 --> 00:27:15.314
which might have been
cloaked ships

00:27:15.359 --> 00:27:16.826
but nothing definite.

00:27:16.860 --> 00:27:19.624
So, what was the first sign
of trouble, Mr. Worf?

00:27:21.164 --> 00:27:22.631
There was no warning.

00:27:23.967 --> 00:27:27.027
A bird-of-prey just de-cloaked
off the port quarter.

00:27:27.070 --> 00:27:29.664
Raise shields.
Arm phasers.

00:27:29.706 --> 00:27:32.140
Commander, another
ship's de-cloaking.

00:27:32.175 --> 00:27:33.767
It's an older battle cruiser.

00:27:33.810 --> 00:27:36.278
She's going after the convoy.

00:27:36.313 --> 00:27:38.941
Bring us about.

00:27:38.982 --> 00:27:41.951
How did you feel
when the Klingons attacked?

00:27:42.019 --> 00:27:43.884
Were you excited?

00:27:43.921 --> 00:27:45.115
Of course.

00:27:45.155 --> 00:27:46.679
I am a Klingon.

00:27:46.723 --> 00:27:48.384
We live for battle.

00:27:48.425 --> 00:27:50.325
So that's all
that mattered to you...

00:27:50.360 --> 00:27:51.554
the chance to fight?

00:27:51.595 --> 00:27:55.326
No, sir. Whatever
my personal feelings may be

00:27:55.365 --> 00:27:58.425
I do not allow them
to interfere with my duty

00:27:58.468 --> 00:27:59.958
or my professional judgment.

00:28:00.070 --> 00:28:02.163
Chief O'Brien says
that he disagrees

00:28:02.205 --> 00:28:03.900
with your decision to fire.

00:28:03.941 --> 00:28:06.739
How do you respond to that?

00:28:06.777 --> 00:28:08.574
I respect the Chief's opinion.

00:28:08.612 --> 00:28:10.842
He and I have served together
for many years

00:28:10.881 --> 00:28:12.644
and I consider him a friend.

00:28:12.683 --> 00:28:15.345
However, he was not
in command that day.

00:28:15.385 --> 00:28:16.909
What difference does that make?

00:28:17.020 --> 00:28:19.045
It makes all the difference.

00:28:19.089 --> 00:28:21.182
He is looking back at a decision

00:28:21.224 --> 00:28:22.919
analyzing it weeks later.

00:28:22.960 --> 00:28:25.121
As the Commanding Officer
of the Defiant

00:28:25.162 --> 00:28:26.925
it was my duty to look forward

00:28:26.964 --> 00:28:29.455
to anticipate
every possible situation.

00:28:29.499 --> 00:28:30.625
Did you anticipate

00:28:30.667 --> 00:28:34.467
encountering a civilian ship
on this mission?

00:28:34.504 --> 00:28:36.938
I knew our convoy
would be passing

00:28:37.040 --> 00:28:38.837
through civilian
shipping lanes, but...

00:28:38.875 --> 00:28:41.605
in my judgment, the chances
of a civilian vessel

00:28:41.645 --> 00:28:44.944
de-cloaking in the middle
of a battle were remote.

00:28:44.982 --> 00:28:48.042
I decided that if I were
engaged in combat

00:28:48.085 --> 00:28:50.918
I would not hesitate
to fire at a de-cloaking ship.

00:28:50.954 --> 00:28:53.855
Mr. Worf, I want you to think

00:28:53.890 --> 00:28:57.587
about the civilians who died
on that transport ship

00:28:57.627 --> 00:28:59.959
and answer one question.

00:28:59.997 --> 00:29:03.194
Under the same set
of circumstances

00:29:03.233 --> 00:29:04.757
would you do it again?

00:29:08.305 --> 00:29:09.670
Yes, sir.

00:29:09.706 --> 00:29:12.641
If I had hesitated,
I would have been negligent.

00:29:12.676 --> 00:29:15.110
I would have been risking
my ship, my crew

00:29:15.145 --> 00:29:16.737
and the entire convoy.

00:29:19.750 --> 00:29:21.809
Thank you.

00:29:23.754 --> 00:29:25.688
Worf...

00:29:25.722 --> 00:29:30.352
why are you considered
an outcast among Klingons?

00:29:30.394 --> 00:29:32.328
I sided with the Federation

00:29:32.362 --> 00:29:34.387
during the invasion
of Cardassia.

00:29:34.431 --> 00:29:36.399
For that, Chancellor Gowron

00:29:36.433 --> 00:29:39.732
stripped me of my name
and my family honor.

00:29:39.770 --> 00:29:42.671
So you acted out of conscience
and you were punished for it.

00:29:42.706 --> 00:29:45.300
How do you feel about that?

00:29:45.342 --> 00:29:47.276
Angry? Bitter?

00:29:47.310 --> 00:29:51.041
I am angry about the treatment
I have received.

00:29:51.081 --> 00:29:53.709
I felt it was unjust.

00:29:53.750 --> 00:29:55.479
Of course you are.

00:29:55.519 --> 00:29:56.679
Who wouldn't be?

00:29:56.720 --> 00:29:59.245
What happened affected
your entire family.

00:29:59.289 --> 00:30:01.780
The House of Mogh
was brought down.

00:30:01.825 --> 00:30:03.588
Your brother was ejected

00:30:03.627 --> 00:30:05.788
from the High Council
in disgrace

00:30:05.829 --> 00:30:07.626
your lands seized

00:30:07.664 --> 00:30:11.122
and now your son, Alexander,
has to bear the stigma

00:30:11.168 --> 00:30:13.500
of being the son of a traitor.

00:30:13.537 --> 00:30:15.368
Did I miss anything?

00:30:16.339 --> 00:30:17.806
No.

00:30:17.841 --> 00:30:19.365
In your opinion

00:30:19.409 --> 00:30:21.900
what do they think of you
in the Empire, Worf?

00:30:21.945 --> 00:30:23.708
I am hated.

00:30:23.747 --> 00:30:25.612
Why?
Because of what you did?

00:30:25.649 --> 00:30:26.638
Yes.

00:30:26.683 --> 00:30:29.277
Are you sure
it's not something more basic?

00:30:30.487 --> 00:30:32.421
What is that supposed to mean?

00:30:34.157 --> 00:30:35.988
Isn't it obvious?

00:30:38.195 --> 00:30:40.390
You were raised by humans

00:30:40.430 --> 00:30:42.694
on Earth

00:30:42.732 --> 00:30:45.530
and now you wear their uniform.

00:30:45.569 --> 00:30:50.006
Haven't you really always been
a traitor in your heart?

00:30:50.040 --> 00:30:51.098
No.

00:30:51.141 --> 00:30:52.369
Are you telling us

00:30:52.409 --> 00:30:55.674
that you live with humans,
but your heart is Klingon?

00:30:55.712 --> 00:30:56.838
Yes.

00:30:56.880 --> 00:30:59.007
But if your heart is Klingon

00:30:59.082 --> 00:31:01.243
how could you fire
upon your own people?

00:31:01.284 --> 00:31:03.115
They fired the first shot.

00:31:03.153 --> 00:31:05.815
And when that happened,
they became my enemies.

00:31:05.856 --> 00:31:08.689
Then why aren't you glad you
destroyed that transport?

00:31:08.725 --> 00:31:11.387
It was filled with your
enemies and their children.

00:31:11.428 --> 00:31:13.259
There is nothing honorable

00:31:13.296 --> 00:31:15.856
about killing those
who cannot defend themselves.

00:31:15.899 --> 00:31:21.064
Are you telling me
that you would never

00:31:21.104 --> 00:31:24.403
attack a defenseless opponent?

00:31:24.441 --> 00:31:27.103
No. I would not.

00:31:32.182 --> 00:31:34.742
Maybe I was wrong about you.

00:31:34.784 --> 00:31:39.084
Maybe you aren't really
Klingon in your heart.

00:31:39.122 --> 00:31:42.717
A true Klingon rejoices
at the death of his enemies...

00:31:42.759 --> 00:31:45.159
old, young, armed, unarmed.

00:31:45.195 --> 00:31:47.993
All that matters is the victory.

00:31:48.031 --> 00:31:49.692
Tell me, Worf...

00:31:49.733 --> 00:31:52.930
did you weep for those children?

00:31:56.540 --> 00:31:58.132
I grieve for them.

00:31:58.175 --> 00:31:59.403
Grieve for them?

00:31:59.442 --> 00:32:01.637
A Klingon does not grieve.

00:32:01.678 --> 00:32:03.669
They died in glorious battle.

00:32:03.713 --> 00:32:05.943
They are with the honored dead
in Sto-Vo-Kor.

00:32:05.982 --> 00:32:07.711
They do not want your grief.

00:32:07.751 --> 00:32:09.150
You dishonor their memory.

00:32:09.186 --> 00:32:10.380
Objection.

00:32:10.420 --> 00:32:11.944
Advocate.

00:32:11.988 --> 00:32:13.285
You will say anything.

00:32:13.323 --> 00:32:15.450
You have no honor.

00:32:15.492 --> 00:32:17.790
I say this...
you live with humans

00:32:17.827 --> 00:32:20.455
because you're afraid
to live with Klingons.

00:32:20.497 --> 00:32:22.431
I fear nothing

00:32:22.465 --> 00:32:24.524
and if you would like
to pick up a bat'leth

00:32:24.568 --> 00:32:26.627
and face me with weapons
instead of words

00:32:26.670 --> 00:32:27.967
I will prove it to you.

00:32:28.071 --> 00:32:29.504
You'd like that,
wouldn't you, Worf?

00:32:29.539 --> 00:32:31.370
You'd love to prove
that you are as strong

00:32:31.408 --> 00:32:33.239
and courageous
as any Klingon warrior.

00:32:33.276 --> 00:32:35.369
I am a Klingon warrior.

00:32:35.412 --> 00:32:37.073
Advocate, you are stepping

00:32:37.113 --> 00:32:39.081
well beyond
the bounds of protocol.

00:32:39.115 --> 00:32:40.878
And that is why
you told the Ferengi

00:32:40.917 --> 00:32:42.646
you hope the Klingons
do come for you.

00:32:42.686 --> 00:32:45.348
You wanted to prove
yourself in the eyes

00:32:45.388 --> 00:32:46.855
of the only people
that matter to you...

00:32:46.890 --> 00:32:48.482
other Klingons!

00:32:48.525 --> 00:32:51.892
This will stop, or I will hold
both of you in contempt.

00:32:54.598 --> 00:32:56.589
I apologize, Worf.

00:32:59.436 --> 00:33:01.495
Actually...

00:33:01.538 --> 00:33:03.267
I pity you.

00:33:03.306 --> 00:33:07.043
But the person I pity most
is Alexander...

00:33:07.176 --> 00:33:11.442
because one day,
he will come to you and ask

00:33:11.480 --> 00:33:14.278
"Father, who am I?"

00:33:14.316 --> 00:33:16.113
And you will have to tell him

00:33:16.152 --> 00:33:19.815
that he is the son
of a small, frightened man

00:33:19.855 --> 00:33:22.722
who destroyed
a ship full of children

00:33:22.758 --> 00:33:24.953
just to prove his own courage.

00:33:25.061 --> 00:33:26.619
Worf, no!

00:33:38.140 --> 00:33:44.568
I thought you told me you'd
never attack an unarmed man.

00:33:47.616 --> 00:33:49.982
Perhaps you should have said

00:33:50.052 --> 00:33:52.179
"not unless I get angry."

00:33:54.190 --> 00:33:59.093
"Not unless I have
something to prove."

00:33:59.128 --> 00:34:01.062
I rest my case.

00:34:17.813 --> 00:34:22.273
Captain's Log, Stardate 49665.3.

00:34:22.318 --> 00:34:25.116
The hearing is in recess
and Admiral T'Lara

00:34:25.154 --> 00:34:28.351
has retired to her quarters
to begin deliberations.

00:34:28.390 --> 00:34:31.223
I wish I could be more
optimistic about her decision.

00:34:32.828 --> 00:34:34.227
Constable.

00:34:35.531 --> 00:34:37.089
Good news.

00:35:02.158 --> 00:35:03.591
Captain Sisko.

00:35:03.626 --> 00:35:06.220
Admiral, I apologize

00:35:06.262 --> 00:35:08.253
for interrupting
your deliberations

00:35:08.297 --> 00:35:11.027
but I have some new evidence
I'd like to present.

00:35:11.066 --> 00:35:12.931
Very well.

00:35:12.968 --> 00:35:17.667
I'd like Advocate Ch'Pok
to evaluate the evidence

00:35:17.706 --> 00:35:20.607
as an expert witness
on the Klingon Empire.

00:35:20.643 --> 00:35:24.238
I will not compel you
to testify, Advocate.

00:35:29.018 --> 00:35:31.009
Care to step
onto my battlefield?

00:35:42.398 --> 00:35:47.062
Advocate, how would you describe
the current relationship

00:35:47.102 --> 00:35:49.832
between the Federation
and the Klingon Empire?

00:35:49.872 --> 00:35:53.968
There is no formal relationship
between our two governments.

00:35:54.043 --> 00:35:55.977
What would you call us?

00:35:56.045 --> 00:35:59.344
Informal friends?
Informal enemies?

00:35:59.381 --> 00:36:00.348
I would say

00:36:00.382 --> 00:36:03.078
there is potential
for either label.

00:36:03.118 --> 00:36:06.349
But at the moment,
neither is entirely accurate.

00:36:06.388 --> 00:36:08.219
Hmm, interesting.

00:36:08.257 --> 00:36:09.918
Would you agree that,
at the moment

00:36:10.025 --> 00:36:12.789
it is difficult for us
to trust each other?

00:36:12.828 --> 00:36:15.661
Difficult, but not impossible.

00:36:15.698 --> 00:36:18.861
There are things that transcend
our differences.

00:36:18.901 --> 00:36:22.098
For example, we trust
that this case

00:36:22.137 --> 00:36:23.695
can be decided fairly.

00:36:23.739 --> 00:36:27.368
We have faith
in Admiral T'Lara's judgment.

00:36:27.409 --> 00:36:29.468
Oh, I'm glad to hear you have

00:36:29.511 --> 00:36:33.379
such a profound respect
for the Admiral.

00:36:33.415 --> 00:36:37.852
But would it be fair to say
that outside this hearing

00:36:37.886 --> 00:36:40.946
you do not entirely trust us?

00:36:41.056 --> 00:36:46.824
Well, it is only prudent
that we question your motives

00:36:46.862 --> 00:36:49.057
now that we are
no longer allies.

00:36:49.098 --> 00:36:51.191
Of course, and it is only

00:36:51.233 --> 00:36:53.428
prudent of us
to question your motives.

00:36:53.469 --> 00:36:55.061
After all, aren't there times

00:36:55.104 --> 00:36:59.598
when you feel it's in your
best interest to deceive us?

00:36:59.642 --> 00:37:02.202
I object to the question.

00:37:02.244 --> 00:37:04.804
It is vague and hypothetical.

00:37:04.847 --> 00:37:06.781
Well, can you imagine
any circumstance

00:37:06.815 --> 00:37:10.751
in which the Empire
would deceive the Federation?

00:37:10.786 --> 00:37:13.721
I have a poor imagination.

00:37:13.756 --> 00:37:17.123
Let's see what we
can do to spark it.

00:37:18.460 --> 00:37:21.395
Do you recognize these names?

00:37:24.933 --> 00:37:27.902
These are the people who were
killed on board the transport.

00:37:27.936 --> 00:37:29.369
You're positive?

00:37:29.405 --> 00:37:32.499
There are 441 of them.

00:37:32.541 --> 00:37:35.374
The names and faces
of these people

00:37:35.411 --> 00:37:37.606
are seared into my heart.

00:37:37.646 --> 00:37:39.637
This is a list of heroes

00:37:39.682 --> 00:37:41.843
who died at the hands
of a coward.

00:37:41.884 --> 00:37:44.876
It is a list I can never forget.

00:37:44.920 --> 00:37:48.947
They are an interesting group
of people, aren't they?

00:37:48.991 --> 00:37:50.891
From every walk of life...

00:37:50.926 --> 00:37:55.556
merchants, soldiers,
artists, shopkeepers...

00:37:55.597 --> 00:37:59.658
- Children.
- Children.

00:37:59.702 --> 00:38:03.160
We've done some checking
in their backgrounds

00:38:03.205 --> 00:38:04.695
and in our opinion

00:38:04.740 --> 00:38:07.038
they all appear to be
a random group of people

00:38:07.076 --> 00:38:09.567
who shared only one thing
in common:

00:38:09.611 --> 00:38:12.739
They all traveled
on the same ship.

00:38:12.781 --> 00:38:14.908
Is that your conclusion as well?

00:38:14.983 --> 00:38:16.507
Yes.

00:38:16.552 --> 00:38:18.747
And it was just fate

00:38:18.787 --> 00:38:23.224
that led these particular people
to board a doomed ship?

00:38:23.258 --> 00:38:26.921
Fate is a human concept.

00:38:26.995 --> 00:38:31.864
They simply boarded the wrong
ship at the wrong time.

00:38:31.900 --> 00:38:34.733
And then... they did it again.

00:38:36.205 --> 00:38:39.265
I don't, uh...
think I understand

00:38:39.308 --> 00:38:40.866
your line of...

00:38:40.909 --> 00:38:42.467
Three months ago

00:38:42.511 --> 00:38:45.309
a Klingon transport ship
crashed

00:38:45.347 --> 00:38:47.338
in the mountains
of Galorda Prime.

00:38:47.383 --> 00:38:49.374
Of course, everyone
assumed the worst...

00:38:49.418 --> 00:38:52.353
that the passengers and the crew
had all been killed.

00:38:52.388 --> 00:38:54.948
But then, miraculously...

00:38:54.990 --> 00:38:57.788
everyone survived.

00:38:57.826 --> 00:39:00.693
Do you know anyone
who was on that ship?

00:39:02.965 --> 00:39:04.296
No.

00:39:04.333 --> 00:39:05.766
Are you sure?

00:39:05.801 --> 00:39:08.929
You have the names
of the survivors right there.

00:39:12.174 --> 00:39:16.110
I can understand your confusion.

00:39:16.145 --> 00:39:19.444
The names in front of you
are identical

00:39:19.481 --> 00:39:22.609
to the names on this list.

00:39:22.651 --> 00:39:26.143
The people who were killed
in the Defiant incident.

00:39:26.188 --> 00:39:29.624
So what does this mean?

00:39:30.993 --> 00:39:37.330
441 people somehow survived
a crash on Galorda Prime.

00:39:37.366 --> 00:39:39.300
And then a few weeks later

00:39:39.334 --> 00:39:43.896
they all decide to take
another trip on the same day

00:39:43.939 --> 00:39:48.069
on the same transport ship,
under the same Captain and crew.

00:39:48.110 --> 00:39:50.078
And then that ship
is destroyed, too.

00:39:50.112 --> 00:39:55.379
This is a very unlucky group
of people, wouldn't you say?

00:39:55.417 --> 00:39:59.911
I am not an expert on luck.

00:39:59.955 --> 00:40:04.255
No. You are an expert
on the Klingon Empire.

00:40:04.293 --> 00:40:07.694
So, tell me, Advocate

00:40:07.729 --> 00:40:10.823
isn't it possible
that there were no civilians

00:40:10.866 --> 00:40:13.130
on the transport Worf destroyed?

00:40:13.168 --> 00:40:16.194
Isn't it possible
that the ship he saw

00:40:16.238 --> 00:40:18.934
was sending out
false sensor images

00:40:18.974 --> 00:40:21.442
and that this whole affair
was staged

00:40:21.477 --> 00:40:25.012
so that the only Klingon
officer in Starfleet

00:40:25.145 --> 00:40:27.272
would be accused of a massacre,
and the Federation

00:40:27.314 --> 00:40:30.943
would be forced to stop
escorting the convoys?

00:40:30.984 --> 00:40:34.750
Tell me, Advocate...

00:40:36.256 --> 00:40:40.192
isn't it possible?

00:40:44.865 --> 00:40:46.924
Yes.

00:41:04.384 --> 00:41:06.511
Captain.

00:41:06.553 --> 00:41:08.111
I thought you should know

00:41:08.155 --> 00:41:10.953
O'Brien and Bashir are throwing
a party for you at Quark's.

00:41:10.991 --> 00:41:13.050
Looks like quite a bash.

00:41:13.093 --> 00:41:14.958
I am aware of it.

00:41:15.062 --> 00:41:17.622
But I have much on my mind.

00:41:17.664 --> 00:41:19.564
Ch'Pok was right.

00:41:19.599 --> 00:41:21.533
I did have something to prove

00:41:21.568 --> 00:41:23.866
when I took command
of the convoy.

00:41:23.904 --> 00:41:26.702
And I did not realize it

00:41:26.740 --> 00:41:30.232
until I stood there,
looking down at him

00:41:30.277 --> 00:41:33.303
blood trickling from his mouth.

00:41:33.346 --> 00:41:35.940
In that moment,
I remember thinking

00:41:35.982 --> 00:41:39.213
finally, he had given me
what I really wanted...

00:41:39.252 --> 00:41:42.346
a reason to attack him.

00:41:42.389 --> 00:41:44.653
And I had that same feeling

00:41:44.691 --> 00:41:46.750
when the Klingon ships
first attacked.

00:41:46.793 --> 00:41:50.661
Finally, a chance for vengeance.

00:41:54.101 --> 00:41:56.501
I should not have
accepted the mission.

00:41:56.536 --> 00:41:59.164
I am glad you realize that.

00:42:04.644 --> 00:42:06.908
That was your first mistake.

00:42:06.947 --> 00:42:08.778
What was your second?

00:42:10.851 --> 00:42:12.785
When the ship de-cloaked

00:42:12.819 --> 00:42:15.049
I should have checked
the target before I fired.

00:42:15.088 --> 00:42:17.113
You're damned right
you should have checked.

00:42:17.157 --> 00:42:19.318
You knew there were
civilian ships in the area.

00:42:19.359 --> 00:42:21.884
You fired at something
you hadn't identified.

00:42:26.233 --> 00:42:31.637
You made a military decision
to protect your ship and crew.

00:42:31.671 --> 00:42:34.834
But you're
a Starfleet officer, Worf.

00:42:34.875 --> 00:42:37.969
We don't put civilians at risk,
or even potentially at risk

00:42:38.011 --> 00:42:39.979
to save ourselves.

00:42:40.046 --> 00:42:42.412
Sometimes that means
we lose the battle

00:42:42.449 --> 00:42:44.917
and sometimes our lives.

00:42:44.951 --> 00:42:47.852
But if you can't make
that choice

00:42:47.888 --> 00:42:51.380
then you can't wear
that uniform.

00:42:51.424 --> 00:42:53.824
Yes, sir.

00:42:53.860 --> 00:42:55.623
At ease, Commander.

00:42:59.366 --> 00:43:02.631
Now, all that being true

00:43:02.669 --> 00:43:05.399
the reality is
no harm's been done.

00:43:05.438 --> 00:43:09.465
There are no dead children
on your conscience.

00:43:09.509 --> 00:43:10.874
You got lucky.

00:43:13.113 --> 00:43:15.741
I do not feel lucky.

00:43:15.782 --> 00:43:18.307
And that's why, despite
everything that's happened

00:43:18.351 --> 00:43:21.843
you're going to make
a hell of a Captain someday.

00:43:21.888 --> 00:43:23.355
Now, let's go.

00:43:23.390 --> 00:43:24.379
They'll all be waiting.

00:43:27.194 --> 00:43:32.826
Look, this party isn't for you
as much as it is for them.

00:43:32.866 --> 00:43:35.494
Things got a little tense
there for a while.

00:43:35.535 --> 00:43:37.560
They need a release,
a chance to celebrate.

00:43:38.605 --> 00:43:41.802
But I do not feel
like celebrating.

00:43:41.841 --> 00:43:45.106
Part of being a Captain
is knowing when to smile.

00:43:45.145 --> 00:43:47.773
Make the troops happy...
even when it's

00:43:47.814 --> 00:43:50.305
the last thing in the world
you want to do.

00:43:50.350 --> 00:43:52.614
Because they're your troops

00:43:52.652 --> 00:43:55.678
and you have
to take care of them.

00:43:57.857 --> 00:44:01.918
Life is a great deal more
complicated in this red uniform.

00:44:01.962 --> 00:44:04.487
Wait till you get
four pips on that collar.

00:44:04.531 --> 00:44:08.058
You'll wish you had gone
into botany.
